            "text": "Scammers employ **impersonation** (e.g., posing as police, financial institutions) and **urgency-driven tactics** to extract sensitive information. They use **persuasive cues** (e.g., fabricated legitimacy, pressure) to lower victim suspicion during mid-stages of the scam. Key vulnerabilities include susceptibility to **persuasive cues** in Stage 3 and the lack of adaptive warnings to counter **escalating pressure** in later stages.",
