            "embedding_text": "Authority: Social_Engineering\n\n        Document: 2601.13581v1\n\n        Chapter:\n        \n        \n\n        Section:\n        \n\n        Heading:\n        \n\n        Content:\n\n        Scammers employ **impersonation** (e.g., posing as police, financial institutions) and **urgency-driven tactics** to extract sensitive information. They use **persuasive cues** (e.g., fabricated legitimacy, pressure) to lower victim suspicion during mid-stages of the scam. Key vulnerabilities include susceptibility to **persuasive cues** in Stage 3 and the lack of adaptive warnings to counter **escalating pressure** in later stages."
